# Quality

- Treat compiler warnings as errors in practice. Do not leave `dead_code`, `unused`, or similar warnings.
- After substantive edits, run `cargo test` (or at least `cargo check`) and clear every warning before finishing.
- Prefer deleting unused code over `#[allow(...)]`. Allow only when the unused item is required by an external API or a near-term intentional stub, and keep the allow narrowly scoped with a one-line reason.
- Do not introduce unused imports, functions, methods, or variables “for later.”
